        "id": "527005",
        "date_added": "2026-11-16 20:03:42",
        "twitter_handle": null,
        "display_name": null,
        "comment": "EFN ghost client 1.2.0 (fabric.mod.json id 'efn', https://efn.lol) - Minecraft Fabric client mod carrying a SilentNET infostealer payload. Fake-Fabric shape: 8 obfuscated classes directly under net/fabric/ (not net/fabricmc/), Fabric entrypoint net.fabric.kgtqfrmPool (ModInitializer). On game start it collects Minecraft username, UUID, session accessToken, joined server domain and gameDir into JSON, Base64-encodes it and exfiltrates it. C2 config is resolved from a Polygon blockchain smart contract via eth_call RPC (EtherHiding); a fake-PNG steganographic second stage is downloaded from thisisafalsepositive.st/cdn/ and executed with a portable Python runtime staged in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Microsoft\\Windows\\NtProfileIndex\\ (disguised as a Windows component, launched via javaw.exe). Raw-socket HTTPS with DNS-over-HTTPS (cloudflare-dns.com) fallback. All payload strings are decrypted at runtime via char arithmetic ((char)(a^b) and Hangul char-subtraction), so the constant pool contains zero plaintext IOCs - the reason quick static scanners show it clean. Attributed purely by static analysis (Vineflower decompilation + manual char-arithmetic decoding), never executed. TTPs match published SilentNET research: Malwation 'Inside SilentNET' (2026-10), Broadcom 'SilentNet - RAT/Stealer masquerading as a Minecraft hack client' (2026-06), abuse.ch YARA fake-fabric-mod rules. Related SilentNet build (meteor-addon encrypted-payload shape): sha256 205a1d2a70479e533131139c8a3f7829fcd1abe060fccbd3b00e07fb4308d0a7."
      }
